# Copy to .env.local (dev) or set in your host's environment variables (prod).

# Required. The GitHub repo whose Releases are the launcher's update source.
# Publishing a (non-draft, non-prerelease) release there is what triggers
# every installed launcher to pick up the update — no website redeploy.
GITHUB_REPO=owner/arcane-launcher

# Optional. Raises GitHub's API limit from 60/h to 5000/h. A fine-grained
# token with read-only access to public repos is enough.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional. Shown as a "Discord" link in the footer. Must be an https:// invite
# URL. Leave it out and no Discord link appears. (The GitHub link comes from GITHUB_REPO above.)
# These are read when the site is built, so redeploy after changing them.
# DISCORD_INVITE_URL=https://discord.gg/your-invite

# ---- News from Sanity (see studio/README.md) ----------------------------------
# Optional. Without SANITY_PROJECT_ID the news pages are empty. With it, posts
# published in the Studio appear.
# From https://www.sanity.io/manage -> your project -> Project ID.
# SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# SANITY_DATASET=production

# Optional. Only if the dataset is private. A read-only token from
# sanity.io/manage -> API -> Tokens (Viewer).
# SANITY_READ_TOKEN=

# Optional but recommended. Makes a publish show up on the site immediately
# instead of within a minute. Any long random string; then add a Sanity webhook
# (sanity.io/manage -> API -> Webhooks) that POSTs to
#   https://<your-site>/api/revalidate?secret=<the same string>
# on create, update and delete of "post" documents.
# SANITY_REVALIDATE_SECRET=
